# Four fixed offline static scans across actual owned Git revisions. No provider calls.
name: Real Git revisions retain human review, absence and report source history
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/git_review_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
paste-file: @ART/open.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 AWS Access Key | baseline-review
submit: decision confirmed Owned documentation example reviewed on baseline
require-live-snap: 25 No later observation | baseline-decision
expect: recorded: confirmed
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/git_review_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART committed
submit: findings
paste-file: @ART/open.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 different commit | changed-commit
expect: git-base
expect: git-committed
expect: Reassess this verdict
ask: Does Review retain the human verdict while clearly identifying two actual commits, even though the cited file is unchanged?
submit: runs diff git-base git-committed
require-live-snap: 25 SEEN AGAIN | committed-comparison
expect: Absence does not establish a fix.
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 20 content: | committed-source-identities
expect: main, clean
expect-not: content:unknown
keys: Escape
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/git_review_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART dirty
submit: runs diff git-committed git-dirty
require-live-snap: 25 SEEN AGAIN | dirty-comparison
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 20 main, dirty | dirty-source-identities
expect: main, clean
expect-not: content:unknown
ask: Does comparison show the same full SHA with distinct captured content and clean versus dirty states, without claiming a fix?
keys: Escape
submit: findings
paste-file: @ART/open.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 DECISION SOURCE | dirty-review
expect: Reassess this verdict
resize: 160x48
live-snap: review-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: review-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: review-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: review-60x20
nav-mode:
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 q review list | selected-reader
expect: F-0001 · FINDING
resize: 40x12
live-snap: review-40x12
expect-not: Enter DFD
expect: PgUp/PgDn
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-page-1
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-page-2
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-page-3
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-page-4
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-page-5
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-page-6
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-page-7
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-page-8
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-page-9
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-page-10
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/git_review_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART captured-history
ask: At all six sizes, can the operator inspect the retained verdict, original source and later dirty observation without losing the selected finding?
resize: 120x36
submit: decision deferred Owned dirty revision deliberately deferred
nav-mode:
keys: g
require-live-snap: 25 Owned dirty revision deliberately deferred | dirty-decision
expect: recorded: deferred
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/git_review_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART gap
submit: findings
paste-file: @ART/open.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 not observed | retained-gap
expect: recorded: deferred
expect: Absence does not establish a fix.
ask: Does the fourth planned scan retain the finding and human decision when the documentation example is absent, with no fixed or removed state?
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 Enter export | report
keys: j j j
require-live-snap: 20 format json | json-format
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 EXPORTED | exported
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/git_review_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART exported
ask: Do local JSON, confirmed SARIF and Markdown exports carry the recorded full SHAs and dirty states, while disclosing that current-checkout applicability was not assessed?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/open.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Owned dirty revision deliberately deferred | recovered-review
expect: not observed
resize: 40x12
live-snap: no-color-40x12
expect-not: Enter DFD
resize: 120x36
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 Enter export | recovered-report
require-live-snap: 25 1 finding · 1 reviewed | recovered-report-ready
expect: Scope: workspace history
expect: Workspace spend: total unavailable
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/git_review_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART recovered
ask: Does no-color restart retain exactly four scans, three observations and two human decisions without more discovery or source changes?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
